{"name":"Powder Mill","hex":"#9cb3b5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"powder mill","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["mill that manufactures black powder (type of gunpowder)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/powder_mill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Powder mill","blocks":[{"text":"A powder mill was a mill where gunpowder is made from sulfur, saltpeter and charcoal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Encyclop%C3%A9die_-_illustration_of_a_powder-mill_%2818th_Century%29.jpg/330px-Encyclop%C3%A9die_-_illustration_of_a_powder-mill_%2818th_Century%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powder_mill"},{"title":"Powder","blocks":[{"text":"A powder is a dry solid composed of many very fine particles that may flow freely when shaken or tilted. Powders are a special sub-class of granular materials, although the terms powder and granular are sometimes used to distinguish separate classes of material. In particular, powders refer to those granular materials that have the finer grain sizes, and that therefore have a greater tendency to form clumps when flowing. Granulars refer to the coarser granular materials that do not tend to form clumps except when wet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Iron_powder.JPG/330px-Iron_powder.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powder"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Hagley_Mill_Equipment.jpg/500px-Hagley_Mill_Equipment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Hagley_Mill_Equipment.jpg/500px-Hagley_Mill_Equipment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A working example of the drawing above. This is a restored edge-runner mill at Eleutherian Mills.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHagley_Mill_Equipment.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Orange_Powder_Mill_ruins.jpg/500px-Orange_Powder_Mill_ruins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Orange_Powder_Mill_ruins.jpg/500px-Orange_Powder_Mill_ruins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This former Laflin & Rand powder mill building illustrates the protective stone walls on three sides after the weaker wooden back wall and roof have rotted away.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrange_Powder_Mill_ruins.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Microstructure_of_a_steel_powder_particle.jpg/500px-Microstructure_of_a_steel_powder_particle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Microstructure_of_a_steel_powder_particle.jpg/1280px-Microstructure_of_a_steel_powder_particle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Microstructure_of_a_steel_powder_particle.jpg/500px-Microstructure_of_a_steel_powder_particle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Microstructure of a steel powder particle (image 0.15 mm wide)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMicrostructure_of_a_steel_powder_particle.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}